-# Cancellation-latency fix report
-
-## Evidence
-
-The audit at `/home/tnunamak/.tmp/beellama-cancellation-audit.md` established that
-the response reader enqueues a high-priority `SERVER_TASK_TYPE_CANCEL`, while the
-scheduler is the only owner of `slot.release()`. The delay came from `update_slots()`
-continuing through every target decode sub-batch before returning to that queue.
-
-This change adds `server_queue::has_pending_high_priority_cancel()` and checks it at
-the completed-sub-batch boundary in `update_slots()`. The checkpoint breaks out to
-the existing per-cycle cleanup; the scheduler then dequeues the cancel and reaches
-the unchanged `slot.release()` path in `process_single_task()`.
-
-## Commands and results
-
-- `cmake --build build --target llama-server -j2` — passed.
-- `cmake --build build --target test-server-cancel-scheduling -j2` — passed.
-- `./build/bin/test-server-cancel-scheduling` — passed.
-- `/usr/bin/ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -R '^test-server-cancel-scheduling$'` — passed (1/1).
-- `git diff --check` — passed.
-- Model-backed cancellation test against the rebuilt service — passed: a 40,001-token
-  prompt was disconnected after 503 ms; BeeLlama logged the cancel on the next queue
-  turn and admitted a probe about 590 ms later. The probe completed over HTTP in
-  1,670 ms instead of waiting for the abandoned prompt.
-- Post-restart semantic smoke test — passed: `Reply with exactly OK` returned `OK`
-  with `finish_reason: stop` in 2.5 seconds.
-
-`test-server-cancel-scheduling` deterministically queues cancellation after the
-first modeled prompt-evaluation sub-batch, asserts that a second sub-batch is not
-run, and asserts that cancellation is handled on the subsequent queue turn.
-
-## Risks and limits
-
-- Cancellation cannot interrupt a decode already dispatched to the CPU or GPU; the
-  bound remains disconnect polling plus one in-flight decode sub-batch and one queue
-  turn.
-- The unit test exercises the scheduler queue contract rather than directly invoking
-  the private `update_slots()` implementation. The model-backed HTTP cancellation test
-  covers that integration boundary against the exact rebuilt executable used by the
-  running service (verified by matching `/proc/<pid>/exe` and build artifact inode).
-- The original temporary audit file is outside the writable workspace, so this
-  repository report contains the completion evidence instead of modifying that file.
